  "usage_note": "The verb is often used with **it** as the subject and a clause after it: *It amazes me that nobody noticed*. To say how you feel, English more often uses the adjective **amazed** (*I was amazed*), and to describe the thing that causes the feeling, **amazing** (*It was amazing*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I amazed when I saw the view.",
      "correct": "I was amazed when I saw the view.",
      "note": "**Amaze** needs an object. To talk about your own feeling, use **be amazed**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I was amazing by the view.",
      "correct": "I was amazed by the view.",
      "note": "The **-ed** form tells how you feel; the **-ing** form describes the thing that surprises you: *The view was amazing*."
    }
  ],
